WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
Welcome to First Customer Experiment. I’m Brian Kennedy

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.200
Jr. Entrepreneurship becomes practical when you identify a

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.080
need, offer something useful and learn from a

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.800
real response. This course takes you through a

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.600
small version of that process. You will investigate

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.600
a problem, define a bounded offer, plan a

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.520
test and record what happens. If a suitable

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.840
agreement is made, you can deliver the work

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.320
and track the money and time involved. If

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.400
a sale is not appropriate, you can use

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.920
a no-payment demonstration or our fictional case. We

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.840
will be honest about the difference between a

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:37.360
compliment, a commitment and cash received. You are

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.600
not required to spend money or produce a

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.320
sale to finish. Your result is a documented

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.760
experiment and a reasoned next step. Begin by

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.160
choosing a group you can appropriately reach and

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.080
one problem you want to understand better.
